IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 6 -- Offences against the State`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 121, 121A, 121B, 121C, 121D, 122, 123, 124, 125, 126, 127, 128,
-- 129, 130, 130A.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Fifteen sections in four families. ss 121 to 124 are about war and force against
-- the Government, the President and Members of Parliament or the Cabinet: waging war
-- (s 121), planning against the President (s 121A) or against authority (s 121B),
-- abetting either (s 121C), omitting to inform of any of them (s 121D), preparing
-- for war (s 122), concealing a design for it (s 123), and assaulting or overawing the
-- President or a Member to compel the exercise of a lawful power (s 124). ss 125 to
-- 127 are the same for a POWER IN ALLIANCE OR AT PEACE with Singapore: waging war,
-- depredation, and receiving the proceeds. ss 128 to 130 are about PRISONERS OF STATE
-- OR WAR: a public servant who lets one escape voluntarily or negligently, and anyone
-- who aids, rescues, harbours or resists the recapture of one. s 130A defines
-- "harbour" for the Chapter.
--
-- ss 121, 121C and 125 carry their own abetment ("or abets the waging of such war";
-- "abets the commission of any of the offences") as a fact on the record. They are not
-- built on the s 107 Abetment record, because what is abetted here is the section's
-- own subject matter and the section makes the abetment a principal offence.
--
-- Every section here is one the s 4A extraterritorial rule reaches for a citizen or
-- permanent resident; agent-compliance.l4 computes that classification from these
-- tests.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. Every section here carries its own sentence.

§§ `Sections 121 to 121B -- War, the President and authority`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 121"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes waging or attempting to wage war against the Government or abetting it under Penal Code 1871 section 121
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Waging war against the Government, attempting to, or abetting the waging of such war. The Illustration -- joining an insurrection -- is waging war.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes waging war against the Government` IF
    so's `wages war against the Government or attempts to wage such war or abets the waging of such war`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 121A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes an offence against the President's person under Penal Code 1871 section 121A
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Planning the death of, hurt to, or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President. The plan is the offence; nothing need be carried out.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an offence against the President` IF
    so's `plans the death of or hurt to or unlawful imprisonment or restraint of the President`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 121B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes an offence against authority under Penal Code 1871 section 121B
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Planning the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore, or the overawing by criminal force of the Government.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an offence against authority` IF
    so's `plans the unlawful deprivation or deposition of the President from the sovereignty of Singapore or the overawing by criminal force of the Government`

§§ `Sections 121C and 121D -- Abetting, and omitting to inform`

-- s 121C makes the abetment of a s 121A or s 121B offence an offence punished as
-- those offences are. s 121D reaches a person who knows or has reason to believe
-- that a s 121, 121A, 121B or 121C offence has been committed and intentionally
-- omits to give information about it which he is legally bound to give. The legal
-- duty to inform is a fact: no other written law is in the source bundle.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 121C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting an offence under Penal Code 1871 section 121A or 121B, under section 121C
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Abetting the commission of a s 121A or s 121B offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting an offence against the President or authority` IF
    so's `abets the commission of an offence punishable by section 121A or 121B`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 121D"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes an intentional omission to give information of an offence against the State under Penal Code 1871 section 121D
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Knowing or having reason to believe that a s 121, 121A, 121B or 121C offence has been committed, and intentionally omitting to give information about it which the person is legally bound to give.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes omitting to inform of an offence against the State` IF
        so's `knows or has reason to believe that an offence punishable under section 121 121A 121B or 121C has been committed`
    AND so's `intentionally omits to give information respecting that offence which he is legally bound to give`

§§ `Sections 122 to 124 -- Preparing for war, concealing a design, assaulting the President or a Member`

-- s 122: collecting men, arms or ammunition or otherwise preparing to wage war, with
--   the intention of either waging or being prepared to wage war against the
--   Government. Both the preparation and the intention are required.
-- s 123: concealing, by act or illegal omission, the existence of a design to wage
--   war against the Government, intending the concealment to facilitate the war or
--   knowing it likely to. The concealment is the act; the design is someone's.
-- s 124: with the intention of inducing or compelling the President or a Member of
--   Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise or refrain from exercising a lawful power,
--   assaulting, wrongfully restraining, attempting to restrain, overawing by criminal
--   force or its show, or attempting to overawe, the President or Member. The attempts
--   are inside the section.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 122"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes collecting arms or otherwise preparing to wage war against the Government under Penal Code 1871 section 122
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Collecting men, arms or ammunition, or otherwise preparing to wage war, intending either to wage or to be prepared to wage war against the Government.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes preparing to wage war against the Government` IF
        so's `collects men arms or ammunition or otherwise prepares to wage war`
    AND so's `intends either to wage or to be prepared to wage war against the Government`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 123"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes concealing a design to wage war against the Government under Penal Code 1871 section 123
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Concealing, by any act or illegal omission, the existence of a design to wage war against the Government, intending by the concealment to facilitate the war or knowing it likely that it will.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes concealing a design to wage war` IF
        so's `by any act or illegal omission conceals the existence of a design to wage war against the Government`
    AND so's `intends by the concealment to facilitate or knows it to be likely that the concealment will facilitate the waging of such war`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 124"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assaulting or overawing the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to compel or restrain the exercise of a lawful power under Penal Code 1871 section 124
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Assaulting, wrongfully restraining, overawing by criminal force or its show, or attempting any of these, against the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, intending to induce or compel the exercise or non-exercise of a lawful power.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assaulting or overawing the President or a Member` IF
        so's `intends to induce or compel the President or a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet to exercise or refrain from exercising in any manner any of the lawful powers of the President or such Member`
    AND so's `assaults or wrongfully restrains or attempts wrongfully to restrain or overawes by criminal force or the show of criminal force or attempts so to overawe the President or such Member`

§§ `Sections 125 to 127 -- Powers in alliance or at peace with Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 125"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes waging war against a power in alliance or at peace with Singapore under Penal Code 1871 section 125
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Waging war against the government of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government, attempting to, or abetting the waging of such war.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes waging war against a friendly power` IF
    so's `wages war against the government of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government or attempts to wage such war or abets the waging of such war`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 126"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes committing depredation on the territories of a power in alliance or at peace with Singapore under Penal Code 1871 section 126
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Committing depredation, or making preparations to, on the territories of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government. Forfeiture of the property used or acquired is punishment and is not decided.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes depredation on a friendly power` IF
    so's `commits depredation or makes preparations to commit depredation on the territories of a power in alliance or at peace with the Government`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 127"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes receiving property taken by war or depredation under Penal Code 1871 section 127
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Receiving property knowing it to have been taken in the commission of a s 125 or s 126 offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes receiving property taken by war or depredation` IF
    so's `receives property knowing it to have been taken in the commission of an offence mentioned in section 125 or 126`

§§ `Sections 128 to 130A -- Prisoners of State and prisoners of war`

-- ss 128 and 129 are the custodian's offences: a public servant having custody who
--   voluntarily allows (s 128) or negligently suffers (s 129) the prisoner to escape.
-- s 130 is anyone's: knowingly aiding an escape, rescuing or attempting to rescue,
--   harbouring or concealing an escaped prisoner, or resisting recapture. Its
--   Explanation makes a parolee who goes beyond the limits within which he may be at
--   large an escapee from lawful custody, so that is a second route to "has escaped".
-- s 130A: "harbour" includes supplying shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms,
--   ammunition or means of conveyance, or assisting in any way to evade apprehension.
--   It is encoded as a rule so that the supply fact reaches the harbouring limb.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 128"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape under Penal Code 1871 section 128
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc A public servant having custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war who voluntarily allows the prisoner to escape from the place of confinement.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape` IF
        so's `is a public servant having the custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war`
    AND so's `voluntarily allows the prisoner to escape from the place in which the prisoner is confined`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 129"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war to escape under Penal Code 1871 section 129
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc A public servant having custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war who negligently suffers the prisoner to escape from the place of confinement.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war to escape` IF
        so's `is a public servant having the custody of a prisoner of State or prisoner of war`
    AND so's `negligently suffers the prisoner to escape from the place of confinement in which the prisoner is confined`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130A"
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person harbours the prisoner within section 130A` IF
        so's `harbours or conceals a prisoner of State or prisoner of war`
    OR  so's `supplies the person with shelter food drink money clothes arms ammunition or means of conveyance or assists the person in any way to evade apprehension`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130 Explanation"
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prisoner has escaped from lawful custody within section 130` IF
        so's `the prisoner has escaped from lawful custody`
    OR  so's `the prisoner permitted to be at large on parole within certain limits in Singapore has gone beyond those limits`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes aiding the escape of, rescuing, harbouring or resisting the recapture of a prisoner of State or war under Penal Code 1871 section 130
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence` @desc Knowingly aiding an escape, rescuing or attempting to rescue, harbouring or concealing a prisoner who has escaped (including a parolee beyond his limits), or resisting recapture. Harbouring takes the s 130A meaning.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` IF
        so's `knowingly aids or assists a prisoner of State or prisoner of war in escaping from lawful custody or rescues or attempts to rescue such a prisoner`
    OR  (    `the person harbours the prisoner within section 130A` so
         AND `the prisoner has escaped from lawful custody within section 130` so)
    OR  so's `offers or attempts to offer any resistance to the recapture of such a prisoner`

§§ `The Chapter as a whole`

-- One predicate over the Chapter, for the s 4A classification in agent-compliance.l4.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 121 to 130"
GIVEN so IS A `State Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Chapter 6 offence is made out` IF
        `constitutes waging war against the Government` so
    OR  `constitutes an offence against the President` so
    OR  `constitutes an offence against authority` so
    OR  `constitutes abetting an offence against the President or authority` so
    OR  `constitutes omitting to inform of an offence against the State` so
    OR  `constitutes preparing to wage war against the Government` so
    OR  `constitutes concealing a design to wage war` so
    OR  `constitutes assaulting or overawing the President or a Member` so
    OR  `constitutes waging war against a friendly power` so
    OR  `constitutes depredation on a friendly power` so
    OR  `constitutes receiving property taken by war or depredation` so
    OR  `constitutes voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape` so
    OR  `constitutes negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war to escape` so
    OR  `constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` so

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an offence of war against the Government` IF
        (   `constitutes waging war against the Government` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes preparing to wage war against the Government` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes concealing a design to wage war` (a's `state offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an offence against the President or authority` IF
        (   `constitutes an offence against the President` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes an offence against authority` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes abetting an offence against the President or authority` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes omitting to inform of an offence against the State` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes assaulting or overawing the President or a Member` (a's `state offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an offence against a friendly power` IF
        (   `constitutes waging war against a friendly power` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes depredation on a friendly power` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes receiving property taken by war or depredation` (a's `state offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a prisoner of State or war offence` IF
        (   `constitutes voluntarily allowing a prisoner of State or war to escape` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes negligently suffering a prisoner of State or war to escape` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes aiding rescuing or harbouring a prisoner of State or war` (a's `state offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
